\description{
Owns project datasets, analysis specifications, and results while exposing
the embedded graph through the existing \code{AlphaGraphStore}. A project
snapshot always embeds the current graph-store snapshot.
}
\details{
Snapshots embed the current graph-store snapshot. Dataset and analysis
updates invalidate affected results; graph edits are detected by input hashes.
\verb{$result()} returns only results for current inputs. Use reactive accessors in
a reactive context or inside \code{shiny::isolate()}. Transactions commit project
data; graph changes use the shared \code{graphStore}.
}
